@aymeric-giraudet I've been testing the package to no avail. The codebase is a bit complex and a reproduction on codesandbox might take quite some time. Is there any other way I can share the codebase with you? (it's a client's project so it's not publicly available).

In the meantime, you can see an example at this link https://mecum-auctions-develop.vercel.app/auctions/glendale-2023/lots/

On page load we initialise a RefinementList with a specific value and the URL changes accordingly. However, if you try and refresh the page, the query vars disappear from the URL and the RefinementList previously applied is removed. The same thing happens when you copy/paste the URL with the query vars or if you navigate away and then back to the search results page with the back button of the browser.
